From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Garcia Brisa <d.garciabrisa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:53:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] windows: keep the same-origin policy on in WebView2

Every WebView2 environment started its browser process with
--disable-web-security and --allow-insecure-localhost. With them, any
page an app shows, including remote content in a partition, can read
every other origin's responses: the app's own loopback servers, the
user's intranet, any site the user is signed in to. macOS and Linux
system webviews never turned the policy off, so apps that work there
already send CORS headers where they need them.

Both switches are gone. --allow-insecure-localhost only accepted any
certificate for https://localhost, which no Electrobun scheme uses.
---
 package/src/native/win/nativeWrapper.cpp | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/src/native/win/nativeWrapper.cpp b/package/src/native/win/nativeWrapper.cpp
index 5711826..00051d1 100644
--- a/package/src/native/win/nativeWrapper.cpp
+++ b/package/src/native/win/nativeWrapper.cpp
@@ -8087,9 +8087,7 @@ static std::shared_ptr<WebView2View> createWebView2View(uint32_t webviewId,
                                     nullptr);
                                 
                                 // Add file dialog handler for <input type="file">
-                                // Note: WebView2 generally handles file dialogs automatically,
-                                // but we can enhance support by enabling the necessary permissions
-                                // in the AdditionalBrowserArguments (already done above with --disable-web-security)
+                                // WebView2 handles file dialogs for <input type="file"> itself.
 
                                 // Add download handler - requires ICoreWebView2_4
                                 Microsoft::WRL::ComPtr<ICoreWebView2_4> webview4;
@@ -8262,7 +8260,11 @@ static std::shared_ptr<WebView2View> createWebView2View(uint32_t webviewId,
         // Create WebView2 environment with custom scheme support
         try {
             auto options = Microsoft::WRL::Make<CoreWebView2EnvironmentOptions>();
-            options->put_AdditionalBrowserArguments(L"--disable-features=msWebOOUI,msPdfOOUI,msSmartScreenProtection --allow-insecure-localhost --disable-web-security");
+            // The same-origin policy stays on: --disable-web-security would let
+            // every page read any origin, including the app's own loopback
+            // servers, and --allow-insecure-localhost would accept any
+            // certificate for localhost.
+            options->put_AdditionalBrowserArguments(L"--disable-features=msWebOOUI,msPdfOOUI,msSmartScreenProtection");
 
             // Get the interface that supports custom scheme registration
             Microsoft::WRL::ComPtr<ICoreWebView2EnvironmentOptions4> options4;
